---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

// Keep in step with the code: tracker (packages/tracker/src/g.ts, c.ts), waitlist (apps/edge-api/src/routes/waitlist.ts),
// accounts (apps/edge-api/src/routes/auth.ts) and webhooks. Change this page when what is collected changes.
const UPDATED = '7 November 2026';
const CONTACT = 'support@grosslytics.com';
const h2 = 'mt-12 text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink';
---

<Page title="Privacy policy — Grosslytics" description="What Grosslytics collects on grosslytics.com and in the analytics it provides, why, and how to have it deleted.">
	<main>
		<article class="prose-g mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-5 pt-14 pb-24 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
			<p class="eyebrow mb-3">Legal</p>
			<h1 class="text-[clamp(34px,5vw,48px)] font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[15px] text-ink-3">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

			<p class="mt-8">Grosslytics is run by David Mill (“we”). This policy covers grosslytics.com and the Grosslytics analytics service. Questions or requests: <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Two roles</h2>
			<p>For people who visit grosslytics.com or join our waitlist, we decide what is collected. For the visitors of websites that use Grosslytics, the website owner decides; we, or the owner’s own Cloudflare account when they self-host, only process that data on their behalf. If you visited a site that uses Grosslytics, ask that site’s owner about your data.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>What we collect on grosslytics.com</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Waitlist:</strong> your email address and the plan you chose, so we can write to you once when it opens. We do not send newsletters or share the list.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Accounts (Hosted Cloud, when open):</strong> your email address and a salted hash of your password; never the password itself. Billing is handled by Stripe, which receives your payment details directly; we only store Stripe’s customer and subscription IDs.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Lifetime licenses:</strong> the purchase’s Stripe checkout ID and email, and a hash of your license key.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Our own analytics:</strong> grosslytics.com uses Grosslytics itself, described below.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class={h2}>What the analytics collects</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
				<li>Pages viewed, the referring site or campaign tag, reading time and scroll depth, goals the site defines, and (only on pages with the optional click script) which element was clicked. Typed text is never recorded.</li>
				<li>Country and city, derived by Cloudflare from the connection. IP addresses are not stored.</li>
				<li>Device type, operating system and browser, from the browser’s user agent.</li>
				<li>A random visitor ID in the browser’s local storage and a session ID in session storage. No cookies are set.</li>
				<li>For buyers, from the site owner’s payment provider: the amount, plan, and a hash plus a masked form (such as j***@gmail.com) of the email. The full email is not stored.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="mt-4">Bots and traffic from cloud data centers are discarded. AI crawlers are counted only as totals per page.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Where it is stored</h2>
			<p>On Cloudflare (Workers, D1 and Queues). Hosted data is in our Cloudflare account; self-hosted data is only in the owner’s own account, which we cannot access. Cloudflare may process data in any country where it operates.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>How long</h2>
			<p>Waitlist entries are kept until the plan opens and we have written to you, or until you ask us to delete them. Account data is kept while the account exists. Analytics data is kept until the site owner deletes it.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Your rights</h2>
			<p>You can ask us to see, correct or delete the data we hold about you by writing to <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. We answer within 30 days. Depending on where you live, you may also complain to your data protection authority.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Who else receives data</h2>
			<p>Cloudflare (hosting) and Stripe (payments). We do not sell data or use it for advertising.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Changes</h2>
			<p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes. Material changes will be announced on this page.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Page>
